\subsection{Effects}
\subsubsection{Bag of holding}
Will hold many items without adding their weight to your
   total pack weight.  Does not work correctly, especially do not bless it
   while it is full, but curse it when full.  Also, do not put a bag of
   holding, a bag of tricks, or a wand of cancellation into a bag of holding.
   Both items and contents will blow up.

\subsubsection{Bag of tricks}  
Will allow you to create a monster whenever you activate it.

\subsubsection{Blindfold}  
Makes you blind.  Useful when you have telepathy.

\subsubsection{Bugle}  
Will awaken soldiers on level.  Useful for getting into castle.

\subsubsection{Chest}  
Holds things, but is very heavy.

\subsubsection{Credit card} 
Can be used to open locked doors.

\subsubsection{Crystal ball}  
Can be used to detect things on level.

\subsubsection{Drum}  
Awakens monsters; may scare them away.

\subsubsection{Drum of earthquake}  
Will initiate an earthquake whose intensity depends on
   player level.  That is, it creates random pits.

\subsubsection{Expensive camera}  
Can be flashed at monsters to blind them.  Can also blind
   self (useful if you don't have a blindfold).

\subsubsection{Figurine}  
When activated will provide a tame pet of the same type as the
   figurine.

\subsubsection{Fire horn}  
When played will act as a wand of fire; a ray of flame shoots out
   in desired direction.

\subsubsection{Flute}  
May calm snakes if player has enough dexterity.  Can also be used to
   get into the castle.

\subsubsection{Frost horn}  
When played will act as a wand of cold; a ray of cold shoots out
   in desired direction.

\subsubsection{Harp}  
May calm nymph if player has enough dexterity.  Can also be used to get
   into the castle.

\subsubsection{Horn}  
Will awaken monsters; range depends on player level.  May also scare
   monsters.

\subsubsection{Ice box}  
Will prevent monster corpses from spoiling if they are promptly
   placed within the ice box.

\subsubsection{Key}  
Differently shaped keys will open differently shaped locks.

\subsubsection{Lamp}  
Will light up a room when activated.

\subsubsection{Large box}  
Holds things, but is very heavy.

\subsubsection{Leash}  
Will keep your pet with you, even if you fall through a trapdoor,
   teleport, etc.  However, your pet tends to get in your way more.

\subsubsection{Lock pick}  
Used to open locked doors and chests.

\subsubsection{Magic flute}  
May put monsters to sleep; area of effect depends on player
   level.

\subsubsection{Magic harp}  
Charms monsters; area of effect depends on player level.

\subsubsection{Magic lamp}  
If rubbed, a djinni will appear.  Djinnis from blessed lamps will
   always give wishes; from normal lamps may give a wish (random); from cursed
   lamps they will never give a wish.  May be recharged once with a blessed
   scroll of charging.

\subsubsection{Magic marker}  
Useful for writing graffiti on dungeon floors.  Also can be
   used to write spells on blank scrolls.

\subsubsection{Magic whistle}  
Will teleport all of your pets on the level to the same room
   as you.

\subsubsection{Mirror}  
Can scare some monsters.  Also useful for reflecting gaze attacks.
   Can be used in conjunction with blindfold to determine relative position of
   medusa or Wizard of Yendor.

\subsubsection{Pick-axe}  
Can be used to dig through walls.  Also useful as a weapon.

\subsubsection{Sack}  
Will hold items, freeing inventory space.

\subsubsection{Skeleton key}  
Will open any locked door or chest.

\subsubsection{Stethescope}  
Will tell you stats on creature applied to (HP, level, AC,
   gold, etc.).

\subsubsection{Tinning kit}  
Allows you to tin monster corpses to take with you.  Heavy.

\subsubsection{Tin opener}  
Allows you to open tins easier.

\subsubsection{Whistle}  
When blown, your pets will start heading in your direction.  Other
   monsters may do likewise, though.

\subsection{Identifying Tools}
Once again, make sure that the item is not cursed before playing around with
it.  Most tools are fairly obvious as to their function.  For instance, a
blindfold is always a blindfold, with no other magical properties.  Certain
items (horns, for instance) will have more than one type that appear the same
though.  Here's how you can figure out what they are:

\subsubsection{Bags}  
First of all, drop the bag on the ground and \#loot it.  If you feel
something furry, it's a bag of tricks.  Otherwise, load up until you can't
carry anything more.  Then dump some stuff into the bag (by applying it).  If
you can then pick up more, it's a bag of holding.

\subsubsection{Drums}  
Activate the drum.  If it's a drum of earthquake, you'll know it
immediately from the pits opening up around you.

\subsubsection{Flutes}  
Try playing the flute when you have several monsters around you.  If
they go to sleep, it's a magical flute.

\subsubsection{Harps}  
Try playing the harp when you have several monsters around you.  If
they become charmed (tame), you have a magic harp.

\subsubsection{Horns}  
Activate the horn, tell it to improvise, and give it a direction (if
it asks).  You'll immediately notice the effect if it's magical.

\subsubsection{Keys}  
Try a key on various locks.  If it appears to open all of them, it's
probably a skeleton key.  (Note, however, that a credit card works just as
well, and is lighter.)

\subsubsection{Lamps}  
Try activating the lamp.  If it has no oil, it's a magic lamp.

\subsubsection{Whistles}  
Try blowing it.  If it produces a high whistle, it's normal.  A
wierd whistling will be a magic whistle.

